#: 4da2a75a0ef64897b0b73bde7723c72a
msgid "**Alt disparity** : the barometer altitude disagrees with the inertial navigation (i.e. Baro + Accelerometer) altitude estimate by more than 1 meters.  This message is normally short-lived and can occur when the autopilot is first plugged in or if it receives a hard jolt (i.e. dropped suddenly).  If it does not clear the :ref:`accelerometers may need to be calibrated <common-accelerometer-calibration>` or there may be a barometer hardware issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:283
#: b27cc69e47d0457f94bb14caca482c33
msgid "Compass failures:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:285
#: fa81db6fa1d94f84933a9133c6ee518b
msgid "**Compass X not healthy** : the compass X sensor is reporting that it is unhealthy, which is a sign of a possible hardware failure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:288
#: 8f1731a532b5442c83b579ab72317eff
msgid "**Compass not calibrated** : the :ref:`compass(es) has not been calibrated <common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner>`.  the ``COMPASS_OFS_X, _Y, _Z`` parameters are zero or the number or type of compasses connected has been changed since the last compass calibration was performed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:293
#: c246ebe8c67a4a9c99ff942e92ffcc14
msgid "**Compass offsets too high** : the primary compass's offsets length (i.e. sqrt(x^2+y^2+z^2)) are larger than 500.  This can be caused by metal objects being placed too close to the compass.  If only an internal compass is being used (not recommended), it may simply be the metal in the board that is causing the large offsets and this may not actually be a problem in which case you may wish to disable the compass check."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:301
#: 2c0d5d3196194c5da50842a0284faa4e
msgid "**Check mag field** : This can result from failing two different checks. First, the sensed magnetic field in the area is 35% higher or  lower than the expected value.  The expected length is 530 so it's > 874 or < 185. Also, besides this rough check, when the vehicle's position has been obtained (GPS lock), another check against the field strength predicted using the internal World Magnetic Field database is done with much tighter limits. If you are failing this, either the :ref:`compass calibration <common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner>` has not calculated good offsets and calibration should be repeated, or your vehicle is near a large metallic or magnetic disturbance and will need to be relocated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:305
#: de83852ac0db4d7abf044ee96af5a717
msgid "**Compasses inconsistent** : the internal and external compasses are pointing in different directions (off by >45 degrees).  This is normally caused by the external compasses orientation (i.e. :ref:`COMPASS_ORIENT<COMPASS_ORIENT>` parameter) being set incorrectly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:311
#: 08086b5f0b074e3483e9d443912d2775
msgid "GPS related failures:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:313
#: d03f8eabecce48a1acce5331581893a4
msgid "**GPS Glitch** : the :ref:`GPS is glitching <gps-failsafe-glitch-protection>` and the vehicle is in a flight mode that requires GPS (i.e. Loiter, PosHold, etc) and/or the :ref:`cylindrical fence <common-ac2_simple_geofence>` is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:317
#: ff16f2a3a46c4029bb93b655b5aef23f
msgid "**Need 3D Fix** : the GPS does not have a 3D fix and the vehicle is in a flight mode that requires the GPS and/or the :ref:`cylindrical fence <common-ac2_simple_geofence>` is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:320
#: 9562dd3d375445138245bf66659b0f3a
msgid "**Bad Velocity** : the vehicle's velocity (according to inertial navigation system) is above 50cm/s.  Issues that could lead to this include the vehicle actually moving or being dropped, bad accelerometer calibration, GPS updating at below the expected 5hz."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:325
#: 5310e1e712844a8988cca427366ca795
msgid "**High GPS HDOP** : the GPS's HDOP value (a measure of the position accuracy) is above 2.0 and the vehicle is in a flight mode that requires GPS and/or the :ref:`cylindrical fence <common-ac2_simple_geofence>` is enabled. This may be resolved by simply waiting a few minutes, moving to a location with a better view of the sky or checking sources of GPS interference (i.e. FPV equipment) are moved further from the GPS. Alternatively the check can be relaxed by increasing the :ref:`GPS_HDOP_GOOD<GPS_HDOP_GOOD>` parameter to 2.2 or 2.5.  Worst case the pilot may disable the fence and take-off in a mode that does not require the GPS (i.e. Stabilize, AltHold) and switch into Loiter after arming but this is not recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:337
#: e52e92e62d9d49d79aa95d348babda85
msgid "Note: the GPS HDOP can be readily viewed through the Mission Planner's Quick tab as shown below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:344
#: f434b866f9794b059acf979348491562
msgid "INS checks (i.e. Accelerometer and Gyro checks):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:346
#: 9b9c9746d5d548e7a60d405fde783d92
msgid "**INS not calibrated**: some or all of the accelerometer's offsets are zero.  The :ref:`accelerometers need to be calibrated <common-accelerometer-calibration>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:349
#: 1b231ee8b8f94f61af22576e77547dfc
msgid "**Accels not healthy**: one of the accelerometers is reporting it is not healthy which could be a hardware issue.  This can also occur immediately after a firmware update before the board has been restarted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:353
#: f64ee82b52064ba98683a2e3d7f0dbb1
msgid "**Accels inconsistent**: the accelerometers are reporting accelerations which are different by at least 1m/s/s.  The :ref:`accelerometers need to be re-calibrated <common-accelerometer-calibration>` or there is a hardware issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:357
#: 321d4339d17f4326be213742f6349829
msgid "**Gyros not healthy**: one of the gyroscopes is reporting it is unhealthy which is likely a hardware issue.  This can also occur immediately after a firmware update before the board has been restarted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:361
#: 674843b5d84b417aa5ceb8510cc46691
msgid "**Gyro cal failed**: the gyro calibration failed to capture offsets. This is most often caused by the vehicle being moved during the gyro calibration (when red and blue lights are flashing) in which case unplugging the battery and plugging it in again while being careful not to jostle the vehicle will likely resolve the issue.  Sensors hardware failures (i.e. spikes) can also cause this failure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:368
#: 7a6c7bc1274642ce9cc370d9c6b8d523
msgid "**Gyros inconsistent**: two gyroscopes are reporting vehicle rotation rates that differ by more than 20deg/sec.  This is likely a hardware failure or caused by a bad gyro calibration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:373
#: 73329ee11ff047718d05471326d3206a
msgid "Board Voltage checks:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:375
#: d911012151554e75aac374e2c985c325
msgid "**Check Board Voltage**: the board's internal voltage is below 4.3 Volts or above 5.8 Volts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:378
#: e25338effdd842928ce18851f472eb0e
msgid "If powered through a USB cable (i.e. while on the bench) this can be caused by the desktop computer being unable to provide sufficient current to the autopilot - try replacing the USB cable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:382
#: 09c994b21d244454b660fb2222ba8196
msgid "If powered from a battery this is a serious problem and the power system (i.e. Power Module, battery, etc) should be carefully checked before flying."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:387
#: a6594c3275cd4520a8ad0a1849e1f300
msgid "Parameter checks:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:389
#: ecb2f091ac8547c392adba1a7f543db9
msgid "**Ch7&Ch8 Opt cannot be same**: :ref:`Auxiliary Function Switches <channel-7-and-8-options>` are set to the same option which is not permitted because it could lead to confusion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:391
#: 676a529d929248c59e8c21d87738a55e
msgid "**Check FS_THR_VALUE**: the :ref:`radio failsafe pwm value <radio-failsafe>` has been set too close to the throttle channels (i.e. ch3) minimum."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:393
#: a365aec991b041b3813c3c9ee104d180
msgid "**Check ANGLE_MAX**: the :ref:`ATC_ANGLE_MAX<ATC_ANGLE_MAX>` parameter which controls the vehicle's maximum lean angle has been set below 10 degrees (i.e. 10) or above 80 degrees (i.e. 80)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:397
#: 6def624ccc8b49619e86b44929238c56
msgid "**ACRO_BAL_ROLL/PITCH**: the :ref:`ACRO_BAL_ROLL<ACRO_BAL_ROLL>` parameter is higher than the Stabilize Roll P and/or :ref:`ACRO_BAL_PITCH<ACRO_BAL_PITCH>` parameter is higher than the Stabilize Pitch P value.  This could lead to the pilot being unable to control the lean angle in ACRO mode because the :ref:`Acro Trainer stabilization <acro-mode_acro_trainer>` would overpower the pilot's input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:404
#: 9a05289ea8ec4e86853dd474926b39aa
msgid "Battery/Power Monitor:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:406
#: 88cd59a6d1fb46d48f3efd84d280687a
msgid "If a power monitor voltage is below its failsafe low or critical voltages or failsafe remaining capacity low or critical set points, this check will fail and indicate which set point it is below. It will also fail if these set points are inverted, ie critical point is higher than low point. See :ref:`failsafe-battery` for Copter, :ref:`apms-failsafe-function` for Plane, or :ref:`rover-failsafes` for Rover for more information on these."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-prearm-safety-checks.rst:408
#: 6061c2e428704ae38b287e68e7bf1a30
msgid "In addition, minimum arming voltage and remaining capacity parameters for each battery/power monitor can be set, for example :ref:`BATT_ARM_VOLT<BATT_ARM_VOLT>` and :ref:`BATT_ARM_MAH<BATT_ARM_MAH>` for the first battery, to provide a check that the battery is not only above failsafe levels, but also has enough capacity for operation."
msgstr ""

